	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Teldrassil is the new World Tree of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link}, and the land that grows upon it. It rises from the sea off the northern coast of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, so vast that whole forests, lakes and villages rest on its boughs. At its crown stands the city of {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link}. Its glades are lit by moonwells and watched by the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link}, and to a newcomer it seems the most peaceful place in the world. Those who live there know better. Something is wrong with the tree, and every season the signs grow harder to ignore.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The World Tree",
			text = [=[After the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, the night elves were left without their old strength. {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link} had spent its power to destroy {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link}, and with it the {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link} lost their immortality. {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link} went into the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link} and did not return. In his absence, Arch Druid {link:fandral-staghelm}Fandral Staghelm{/link} took up the leadership of the druids. He persuaded the Circle of Ancients in {link:darkshore}Darkshore{/link} that the time had come to rebuild, and to win back what had been lost. With the Circle's consent, he and the mightiest druids of his order grew a new tree beyond the coast.

When it was grown, Fandral asked the great dragons to bless it, as they had once blessed Nordrassil. Nozdormu, Lord of Time, refused him and rebuked his pride. {link:alexstrasza}Alexstrasza{/link}, the Life-Binder, refused him too. Without their gifts, the growth of Teldrassil has been flawed and unpredictable, and the night elves have not regained their undying lives.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Teldrassil is home to most of the {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link} who survived the war. Young druids, priestesses and {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} begin their service in {link:shadowglen}Shadowglen{/link} and {link:dolanaar}Dolanaar{/link}, then climb to {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link}. Yet the forest is sick. The {link:gnarlpine-furbolgs}Gnarlpine{/link} furbolgs, once gentle friends of the elves, have turned savage. Timberlings rise angry from the soil, bearing tumors. {link:harpies}Harpies{/link} nest about the Oracle Tree, satyrs hide in its caves, and a fel moss spreads through beasts and furbolgs alike. The druids study each new ill in turn. The Arch Druid carries the weight of it all, and he does not carry it lightly.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The night elves.{/b} Druids, priestesses of Elune, {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link}, hunters and craftsfolk, living in villages woven among the trees.
• {b}The {link:gnarlpine-furbolgs}Gnarlpine{/link} furbolgs.{/b} A tribe gone mad, raiding from {link:gnarlpine-hold}Gnarlpine Hold{/link} and the barrow dens.
• {b}Timberlings and grells.{/b} Creatures of the tree itself, many of them corrupted.
• {b}{link:harpies}Harpies{/link} of the Bloodfeather.{/b} They nest in the western glades.
• {b}{link:satyrs}Satyrs{/link}.{/b} A few of these fallen elves lurk in hidden places.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Tree",
			text = [=[• The moonwells of Teldrassil hold waters drawn from the ancient {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link}. The druids use them, the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} revere them as shrines of Elune, and all sorcery is forbidden near them.
• The oldest and strongest moonwell lies beneath the Oracle Tree, which speaks to the elders of the {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link} in its own slow way.
• Plants never seen on the tree before have sprouted there, some from lands as far as the {link:swamp-of-sorrows}Swamp of Sorrows{/link}, and they react strangely with its soil.]=],
		},
	},
})

